---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'CollectionPage',
  name: 'Practical Tools | Mercer Lane Press',
  description: 'Free calculators and practical downloadable tools from Mercer Lane Press.',
  url: 'https://mercerlanepress.com/tools/'
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Practical Tools"
  description="Free calculators and downloadable Excel systems from Mercer Lane Press for construction estimating, performance reviews and recurring HR administration."
  schema={schema}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{name:'Home',href:'/'},{name:'Tools'}]}/>

  <header class="page-head wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">PRACTICAL TOOLS</p>
    <h1>Useful tools for specific problems</h1>
    <p class="lede">Focused calculators and working systems built around the same practical approach as Mercer Lane Press books and guides.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Construction estimating tools</h2>
        <p>Start with a free arithmetic check when you already know the cost base, or use the full Excel estimating spreadsheet when scope, takeoff, cost build-up, review, client output and post-job learning need to stay connected.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">FREE BROWSER CALCULATOR</p>
          <h3><a href="/tools/contractor-markup-margin-calculator/">Contractor Markup &amp; Margin Calculator</a></h3>
          <p>Enter a cost base and either a markup or target margin. See the selling price, profit amount, markup and true margin side by side.</p>
          <p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/contractor-markup-margin-calculator/">Use the free calculator →</a></p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">DOWNLOADABLE MICROSOFT EXCEL SYSTEM</p>
          <h3><a href="/tools/construction-estimating-system-pro/">Construction Estimating Spreadsheet for Contractors — PRO</a></h3>
          <p>A guided scope, takeoff, materials, labour, subcontractor, job-costing, pricing, bid-review, client-proposal and estimate-vs-actual workflow for Microsoft Excel desktop.</p>
          <p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/construction-estimating-system-pro/">Explore the construction estimating spreadsheet →</a></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <h2>Tools support decisions; they do not replace the work behind them</h2>
      <p>A calculator can check arithmetic. A workbook can make assumptions visible. Neither can tell you automatically whether the project scope is complete, whether a labour assumption is realistic, whether a subcontract quotation covers the same work, or whether your business is recovering its costs consistently.</p>
      <p>Where a tool depends on business-specific inputs, use your own current information and appropriate professional advice where needed.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-tint"><div class="wrap"><h2>HR performance review tools</h2><div class="grid-3"><article class="card"><h3><a href="/free-tools/performance-review-template-excel/">Free Performance Review Starter Kit</a></h3><p>An Excel workbook, editable Word form, A4 and US Letter PDFs, and an optional client-side AI Review Prompt Builder. One employee and one review at a time; no signup required.</p><a class="text-link" href="/free-tools/performance-review-template-excel/">Use the free review tool</a></article><article class="card"><h3><a href="/tools/hr-manager-toolkit/">HR Manager Toolkit + AI Productivity System</a></h3><p>31 Excel sheets for recurring HR work, 48 HR prompts and 22 editable form designs. $24.99 USD, one-time purchase.</p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/hr-manager-toolkit/">Explore the complete HR toolkit →</a></article></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
